  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 228 PM CST Fri Nov 13 2026\n\nThe extended forecast will begin as a continuation of the short-term \npattern, as deterministic models keep the region under persistent \nupper-level ridging. This synoptic setup will allow temperatures to \nwarm into the low to mid 60s by Thursday and Friday. Meanwhile, \nbeginning Tuesday, an upper-level Pacific trough will move onshore \nand traverse the western CONUS, with leeside cyclogenesis east of \nthe Rockies by late Wednesday afternoon. As this developing low-\npressure system ejects northeastward out of the Plains, rain showers \nwill overspread the area from the southwest starting Thursday \nmorning as the region enters the system's advancing precipitation \nshield.",
